---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="gegenlesen — two reviewers, a conservative judge" description="Two models read the change. A third keeps only what the lines support. CLI starts the review. Ledger keeps the book.">
	<main class="wrap">
		<section class="hero">
			<div>
				<p class="kicker">PR review on your machine</p>
				<h1>Two readers. One judge. House rules stay off until you flip them.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					<code>gegenlesen review</code> packs the repo. DeepSeek and Gemini both run. Terra keeps or
					drops each finding. Ledger is the shop book, not the front door.
				</p>
				<div class="actions">
					<a class="btn" href="/docs/start">Start a review</a>
					<a class="chip" href="/docs/review">How it works</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<img class="hero-mark" src="/logo.webp" alt="gegenlesen" />
		</section>

		<section class="section" aria-label="Pipeline">
			<h2>Pipeline</h2>
			<div class="pipeline">
				<div class="step"><span>01 pack</span><p>Working tree plus <code>.gegenlesen/diff.patch</code></p></div>
				<div class="step"><span>02 identify</span><p>Git range, then matching enabled rules</p></div>
				<div class="step"><span>03 cheap checks</span><p>Regex, deny-lists, sibling tests on the host</p></div>
				<div class="step"><span>04 two models</span><p>A and B in Docker. Always both.</p></div>
				<div class="step"><span>05 judge</span><p>Keep, drop, or downgrade. Host still checks citations.</p></div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section grid">
			<article class="card">
				<h2>The CLI starts work</h2>
				<p>Ledger never posts a job. You run <code>gegenlesen review</code> from the repo you want read.</p>
			</article>
			<article class="card">
				<h2>Nothing auto-enables</h2>
				<p>Mined and suggested rules land disabled. Accept is a human click.</p>
			</article>
			<article class="card">
				<h2>Learn is a later pass</h2>
				<p>Thumbs and comments sit until you hit learn or the sweeper. Review does not invent rules.</p>
			</article>
			<article class="card">
				<h2>No login</h2>
				<p>Single tenant. Bind loopback. Setup in Ledger writes the OpenRouter key to a gitignored config file.</p>
			</article>
		</section>
	</main>
</Base>
